1
00:00:29,348 --> 00:00:30,474
Jorge.

2
00:00:30,475 --> 00:00:32,934
I showed the photo to my mom earlier.

3
00:00:32,935 --> 00:00:34,102
What did she say?

4
00:00:34,103 --> 00:00:36,272
Primitivo Pascual is his name.

5
00:00:37,356 --> 00:00:41,527
The one on the photo is my grandfather.

6
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:45,073
Let's go?

7
00:00:45,074 --> 00:00:46,074
Let's go.

8
00:00:52,914 --> 00:00:54,040
Let me.

9
00:01:07,136 --> 00:01:08,804
Hold on tight.

10
00:01:08,805 --> 00:01:10,056
Again?

11
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,000
"All the Things I Leave You"
(Episode 5)

12
00:01:48,058 --> 00:01:50,810
I was looking through
the letters last night.

13
00:01:52,479 --> 00:01:53,854
Did you read them?

14
00:01:53,855 --> 00:01:55,273
Not yet.

15
00:01:57,776 --> 00:02:01,780
I spent time analyzing
the post stamps and dates.

16
00:02:08,954 --> 00:02:12,873
There are different kinds of letters.

17
00:02:12,874 --> 00:02:15,209
Some are for his mother.

18
00:02:15,210 --> 00:02:17,671
The others are for your grandpa.

19
00:02:21,675 --> 00:02:25,010
From Hawaii to Ilocos.

20
00:02:25,011 --> 00:02:27,096
But Kiko, look.

21
00:02:27,097 --> 00:02:29,556
It's like they haven't been read.

22
00:02:29,557 --> 00:02:30,599
They're unopened.

23
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:32,644
Huh?

24
00:02:34,854 --> 00:02:36,898
And this one.

25
00:02:38,191 --> 00:02:40,652
It's from your grandpa.

26
00:02:41,861 --> 00:02:44,488
From Ilocos to Hawaii.

27
00:02:44,489 --> 00:02:46,031
It hasn't been read?

28
00:02:46,032 --> 00:02:47,658
Not only that.

29
00:02:47,659 --> 00:02:49,869
It wasn't sent.

30
00:02:51,413 --> 00:02:54,207
It never left the country.

31
00:02:54,958 --> 00:02:57,877
If it wasn't sent...

32
00:03:00,005 --> 00:03:03,133
Then why is it with Grandpa Tino?

33
00:03:05,969 --> 00:03:07,804
I have a feeling...

34
00:03:09,556 --> 00:03:12,474
It was held back.

35
00:03:12,475 --> 00:03:14,310
Oh no.

36
00:03:17,897 --> 00:03:21,067
Our grandfathers were
writing to each other.

37
00:03:22,193 --> 00:03:23,736
But Kiko.

38
00:03:23,737 --> 00:03:26,364
Someone held them back.

39
00:03:28,950 --> 00:03:30,325
Let's read it now.

40
00:03:30,326 --> 00:03:31,326
Can we?

41
00:03:31,327 --> 00:03:32,746
Be patient.

42
00:03:34,789 --> 00:03:38,043
Let me just organize them.

43
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:42,547
Just one.

44
00:03:43,298 --> 00:03:44,674
No.

45
00:04:07,739 --> 00:04:08,864
Mother.

46
00:04:08,865 --> 00:04:11,158
How are things in Ilocos?

47
00:04:11,159 --> 00:04:13,411
It's so different here in Hawaii.

48
00:04:33,014 --> 00:04:35,391
Gather ‘round!

49
00:04:59,833 --> 00:05:02,960
Were you promoted?

50
00:05:02,961 --> 00:05:06,004
This is harder.

51
00:05:06,005 --> 00:05:10,802
I can only rest when I fetch water.

52
00:05:25,066 --> 00:05:28,402
I want to go back to the Philippines.

53
00:05:28,403 --> 00:05:30,445
Are you crazy?

54
00:05:30,446 --> 00:05:34,450
What kind of life is waiting
for us there after the war?

55
00:05:41,082 --> 00:05:43,585
One more?

56
00:06:24,125 --> 00:06:26,543
Did you write everything I said?

57
00:06:26,544 --> 00:06:27,420
Yes.

58
00:06:27,421 --> 00:06:29,922
Did you start with
the magazine I gave you?

59
00:06:29,923 --> 00:06:32,424
You can learn how to read and write.

60
00:06:32,425 --> 00:06:35,845
It's important for the future.

61
00:06:36,888 --> 00:06:39,264
Are you complaining?

62
00:06:39,265 --> 00:06:41,726
That's not what I mean, Tino.

63
00:06:42,227 --> 00:06:44,562
I just care for you.

64
00:06:48,566 --> 00:06:51,318
I already told you, Pablo.

65
00:06:51,319 --> 00:06:54,530
There's someone waiting
for me in San Nicolas.

66
00:07:01,788 --> 00:07:03,915
If Bong was here...

67
00:07:05,833 --> 00:07:09,003
He would know how to read and write.

68
00:07:09,671 --> 00:07:12,465
That's the reason he was not hired here.

69
00:07:15,301 --> 00:07:20,013
They rejected the applications
of anyone who can read and write.

70
00:07:20,014 --> 00:07:22,016
What about you, Pablo?

71
00:07:22,725 --> 00:07:23,934
I'm smart.

72
00:07:23,935 --> 00:07:26,061
I didn't tell them that
I know how to read and write.

73
00:07:26,062 --> 00:07:28,231
I acted like an idiot.

74
00:07:29,148 --> 00:07:30,650
Is that it?

75
00:07:32,068 --> 00:07:34,320
I'm an idiot?

76
00:07:34,946 --> 00:07:36,280
That's not what I meant.

77
00:07:36,281 --> 00:07:39,574
They just don't want
smart people to come here.

78
00:07:39,575 --> 00:07:42,495
Because they think we might start a union.

79
00:07:44,539 --> 00:07:47,582
Those who know how to read and write

80
00:07:47,583 --> 00:07:49,502
have higher positions.

81
00:07:52,630 --> 00:07:54,215
Teach me, Pablo.

82
00:07:55,049 --> 00:07:56,508
It's up to you.

83
00:07:56,509 --> 00:07:57,509
You try.

84
00:07:57,510 --> 00:07:59,553
Me, I'm okay with my position now.

85
00:07:59,554 --> 00:08:01,763
Better than to risk getting fired.

86
00:08:01,764 --> 00:08:03,181
I'll earn for now.

87
00:08:03,182 --> 00:08:04,976
Then I'll return home.

88
00:08:06,686 --> 00:08:09,063
That's also what I said to Bong.

89
00:08:10,106 --> 00:08:13,191
He's waiting for me in San Nicolas.

90
00:08:13,192 --> 00:08:15,402
I know, I know.

91
00:08:15,403 --> 00:08:17,697
I get it that you love Bong.

92
00:08:19,866 --> 00:08:22,368
What was I going to write next?

93
00:08:26,372 --> 00:08:28,124
Put...

94
00:08:30,376 --> 00:08:32,420
I am just here.

95
00:08:34,547 --> 00:08:36,591
I am not giving up.

96
00:08:49,187 --> 00:08:52,147
I had no idea

97
00:08:52,148 --> 00:08:54,942
that life in Hawaii was that hard.

98
00:08:58,154 --> 00:09:01,449
And they said life was good there.

99
00:09:02,325 --> 00:09:06,411
I never thought

100
00:09:06,412 --> 00:09:09,248
it would be hard like that.

101
00:09:17,673 --> 00:09:19,884
One more.

102
00:09:48,079 --> 00:09:49,080
Hand.

103
00:09:51,207 --> 00:09:52,750
How old are you?

104
00:09:55,962 --> 00:09:57,046
Are you a farmer?

105
00:09:58,423 --> 00:10:01,759
How old are you again?

106
00:10:03,344 --> 00:10:04,846
Where are you from?

107
00:10:05,930 --> 00:10:08,306
Do you have relatives in Hawaii?

108
00:10:08,307 --> 00:10:09,975
Tino!

109
00:10:09,976 --> 00:10:12,436
What took you so long?

110
00:10:12,437 --> 00:10:14,564
I had to tell my mother first.

111
00:10:15,273 --> 00:10:16,356
Here.

112
00:10:16,357 --> 00:10:18,608
Empanada.

113
00:10:18,609 --> 00:10:20,862
Don't be angry at me.

114
00:10:23,197 --> 00:10:24,782
Get in line.

115
00:10:26,576 --> 00:10:29,203
I already registered our names.

116
00:10:31,330 --> 00:10:32,706
Bong.

117
00:10:32,707 --> 00:10:36,544
They inspect the hands
of those who register.

118
00:10:49,765 --> 00:10:52,559
What are you looking for there?

119
00:10:52,560 --> 00:10:54,103
Wait.

120
00:10:56,814 --> 00:10:59,567
There are no rocks there.

121
00:11:00,485 --> 00:11:01,776
There are.

122
00:11:01,777 --> 00:11:03,070
Just wait.

123
00:11:18,169 --> 00:11:19,879
Do as I do.

124
00:11:20,922 --> 00:11:22,673
What is this for?

125
00:11:24,926 --> 00:11:28,762
We need to make sure our hands are rough.

126
00:11:28,763 --> 00:11:33,475
So they will accept us.

127
00:11:33,476 --> 00:11:35,603
Where did you learn that?

128
00:11:39,482 --> 00:11:41,526
Just do it.

129
00:11:42,777 --> 00:11:44,111
Do it.

130
00:11:46,322 --> 00:11:47,698
Like this?

131
00:11:49,116 --> 00:11:51,868
Not like that, Bong.

132
00:11:51,869 --> 00:11:53,913
Do it harder.

133
00:11:54,413 --> 00:11:56,666
Let me do it.

134
00:12:22,108 --> 00:12:23,775
Why?

135
00:12:23,776 --> 00:12:25,570
Does it hurt?

136
00:12:29,448 --> 00:12:30,908
No.

137
00:12:49,969 --> 00:12:52,138
Are you happy?

138
00:12:53,973 --> 00:12:59,061
Imagine our lives in Hawaii.

139
00:13:00,646 --> 00:13:02,397
Bong.

140
00:13:02,398 --> 00:13:06,943
We could buy our own land
when we are there.

141
00:13:06,944 --> 00:13:09,404
We can start a business.

142
00:13:09,405 --> 00:13:11,907
We will be together.

143
00:13:13,659 --> 00:13:16,120
Why does it seem like...

144
00:13:17,728 --> 00:13:20,773
you're having second thoughts?

145
00:13:22,918 --> 00:13:24,712
Bong.

146
00:13:25,630 --> 00:13:28,424
This is for our future.

147
00:13:34,722 --> 00:13:37,433
It is not that, Tino.

148
00:13:40,436 --> 00:13:42,605
I have a bad feeling.

149
00:13:46,025 --> 00:13:48,818
The American seemed mad

150
00:13:48,819 --> 00:13:52,823
when he found out I could
write and speak English.

151
00:13:53,866 --> 00:13:56,535
He seemed alright to me.

152
00:14:01,457 --> 00:14:03,917
Bong.

153
00:14:03,918 --> 00:14:06,337
Whatever happens,

154
00:14:08,005 --> 00:14:10,340
we will not be separated.

155
00:14:10,341 --> 00:14:12,677
Okay?

156
00:14:18,140 --> 00:14:20,351
Let's go.

157
00:14:29,318 --> 00:14:30,568
Put that back.

158
00:14:30,569 --> 00:14:32,570
Put them back.

159
00:14:32,571 --> 00:14:33,863
Mother.

160
00:14:33,864 --> 00:14:35,615
I am not going.

161
00:14:35,616 --> 00:14:37,784
Just because Bong was not accepted,

162
00:14:37,785 --> 00:14:39,119
you won't go anymore?

163
00:14:39,120 --> 00:14:42,455
There are a lot of people
who yearn for the glory of Hawaii.

164
00:14:42,456 --> 00:14:45,126
You are wasting your chance.

165
00:14:45,751 --> 00:14:47,252
Mother...

166
00:14:47,253 --> 00:14:50,965
Bong and I promised
that we will go together.

167
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:00,974
Listen to me.

168
00:15:00,975 --> 00:15:02,726
Do this.

169
00:15:02,727 --> 00:15:04,269
For our family.

170
00:15:04,270 --> 00:15:06,354
Not for Bong.

171
00:15:06,355 --> 00:15:07,939
For you.

172
00:15:07,940 --> 00:15:11,527
When you have earned enough,
you can come back home.

173
00:15:25,458 --> 00:15:28,418
I will find a way to write.

174
00:15:28,419 --> 00:15:31,213
Thank you, my child.

175
00:15:33,382 --> 00:15:34,716
Mother.

176
00:15:34,717 --> 00:15:36,926
For Bong.

177
00:15:36,927 --> 00:15:38,261
Not just for you.

178
00:15:38,262 --> 00:15:41,015
For Bong, too.

179
00:15:41,932 --> 00:15:43,892
I will see to it.

180
00:15:43,893 --> 00:15:49,439
I will tell his Grandma Victoria
who works at the post office.

181
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:54,153
I will tell her that you will send letters.

182
00:15:57,031 --> 00:15:59,324
Mother.

183
00:15:59,325 --> 00:16:01,826
Bong, too...

184
00:16:01,827 --> 00:16:04,954
He will be sending letters.

185
00:16:04,955 --> 00:16:08,666
If he tells you to come back,

186
00:16:08,667 --> 00:16:10,001
do not listen to him.

187
00:16:10,002 --> 00:16:13,255
I will not be able to resist him.

188
00:16:15,049 --> 00:16:17,801
I am sure...

189
00:16:17,802 --> 00:16:20,094
He will be writing.

190
00:16:20,095 --> 00:16:25,141
I will personally get it
and mail to the post office.

191
00:16:25,142 --> 00:16:29,020
There will come a day

192
00:16:29,021 --> 00:16:33,567
when you will not regret your decision.

193
00:16:58,008 --> 00:16:59,342
Jorge.

194
00:16:59,343 --> 00:17:01,553
The letter will get wet.

195
00:17:01,554 --> 00:17:03,388
Take it.
I want to stop.

196
00:17:03,389 --> 00:17:04,681
Huh?

197
00:17:04,682 --> 00:17:07,268
I don't want to read anymore.

198
00:17:09,645 --> 00:17:11,105
Okay.

199
00:17:13,482 --> 00:17:15,568
Let's go for a drink?

200
00:17:17,820 --> 00:17:21,407
I wanted to read this one.

201
00:17:22,950 --> 00:17:25,159
The last letter.

202
00:17:25,160 --> 00:17:27,120
But okay...

203
00:17:27,121 --> 00:17:29,790
We can read it next time.

204
00:17:39,550 --> 00:17:43,971
Let's do it.
Now or never.

205
00:17:59,195 --> 00:18:03,449
You read it.

206
00:18:28,182 --> 00:18:31,810
My beloved Bong,

207
00:18:32,768 --> 00:18:37,772
do you still remember the day
we applied for Hawaii?

208
00:18:37,816 --> 00:18:41,904
We were so happy.

209
00:19:32,287 --> 00:19:33,287
Let's go!

210
00:19:33,288 --> 00:19:36,249
We don't want to be
late at the funeral home.

211
00:19:36,250 --> 00:19:39,585
Did you find your mom's favorite dress?

212
00:19:39,586 --> 00:19:41,421
Yes, wait.

213
00:19:41,422 --> 00:19:42,798
I'm coming.

214
00:21:23,732 --> 00:21:28,569
When will you tell your family?

215
00:21:28,570 --> 00:21:30,488
About what?

216
00:21:30,489 --> 00:21:33,283
About the letters.

217
00:21:34,284 --> 00:21:36,661
I won't tell them.

218
00:21:36,662 --> 00:21:38,372
Why not?

219
00:21:40,249 --> 00:21:43,544
They won't understand it.

220
00:21:44,211 --> 00:21:48,382
They have the right to know, Jorge.

221
00:21:50,801 --> 00:21:55,389
I don't want Grandpa
Tino's name to be tainted.

222
00:21:57,349 --> 00:22:02,146
Why, did he do anything wrong?

223
00:22:07,526 --> 00:22:13,781
It's better they remember him in death

224
00:22:13,782 --> 00:22:17,286
as how they knew him when he was alive.

225
00:22:18,996 --> 00:22:20,830
Jorge.

226
00:22:20,831 --> 00:22:23,208
That's history.

227
00:22:23,667 --> 00:22:29,213
We should never forget.

228
00:22:29,214 --> 00:22:32,551
You act like you're not Filipino, Kiko.

229
00:22:33,177 --> 00:22:38,891
Filipinos have selective memory.

230
00:22:39,235 --> 00:22:42,614
They want good vibes all the time.

231
00:22:44,605 --> 00:22:45,771
Why?

232
00:22:45,772 --> 00:22:48,649
Grandpa Tino had a happy life.

233
00:22:48,650 --> 00:22:50,194
Happy?

234
00:22:50,736 --> 00:22:52,195
They separated.

235
00:22:52,196 --> 00:22:55,866
And they never saw each other again.

236
00:22:58,243 --> 00:23:02,080
- There were happy moments.
- What's happy about that?

237
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:05,167
There were happy moments.

238
00:23:05,667 --> 00:23:07,294
When they were together.

239
00:23:12,216 --> 00:23:13,467
Kiko.

240
00:23:14,092 --> 00:23:18,472
Where is your Grandpa Bong?

241
00:23:19,973 --> 00:23:21,849
He's dead.

242
00:23:21,850 --> 00:23:23,393
How did he die?

243
00:23:24,811 --> 00:23:26,104
He was killed.

244
00:23:29,816 --> 00:23:32,319
My mom said...

245
00:23:34,613 --> 00:23:38,575
Grandpa was a leader
of the farmers back then.

246
00:23:39,243 --> 00:23:43,331
They fought those who stole their lands.

247
00:23:43,885 --> 00:23:45,803
That's why...

248
00:23:45,827 --> 00:23:47,330
they shot him.

249
00:23:47,354 --> 00:23:50,649
But that was a long time ago.

250
00:23:55,133 --> 00:24:00,472
I think when they didn't
hear from each other,

251
00:24:02,683 --> 00:24:05,560
they married other people.

252
00:24:06,828 --> 00:24:08,579
Maybe.

253
00:24:08,734 --> 00:24:10,985
Then...

254
00:24:11,066 --> 00:24:14,777
Grandpa Bong moved to Cagayan

255
00:24:14,778 --> 00:24:20,491
when his application
to Hawaii was rejected.

256
00:24:20,492 --> 00:24:22,703
We're not like you, Jorge.

257
00:24:23,537 --> 00:24:26,373
We didn't become rich.

258
00:24:45,475 --> 00:24:46,642
Hello, Auntie.

259
00:24:46,643 --> 00:24:50,646
Kiko, a letter arrived for you.

260
00:24:50,647 --> 00:24:53,607
I couldn't resist opening it.

261
00:24:53,608 --> 00:24:55,818
You passed your scholarship.

262
00:24:55,819 --> 00:24:58,863
- Jorge, I passed.
- Come home quick!

263
00:24:58,864 --> 00:24:59,864
Bye!

264
00:25:41,031 --> 00:25:43,241
Tino.
